\n
\n
\nYOU MAY CATCH A BAD CASE OF DEATH IF YOU DON'T KNOW WHAT YOU'RE DOING
\nEFUN TECHNOLOGIES IS NOT RESPONSIBLE FOR ANY INJURY, ILLNESS, LOSS OF PROPERTY OR LIFE
"
,,40)
}
RESETCOLOR
FONTREGULAR
PRINTFORMW That's not concerning, no?
PRINTFORMW You look at the other page
{
CALL PRINT_LETTER(
@"--- CONTENTS ---
\nPlease check if you've received the following items in your AHE-0005M4 package:
\n・ACM-6310M2 - eShot by eFun Actmix ACM-6310M2 1080p Camera with stand
\n・KIERA 5229335-32G - Kiera Ultra Pro TFLP (TransFlash Long Play) 32GB memory card
\n・ESG-440AM8 - Glass jars with lids (3x)
\n・UWC 64-321-7755-07B - Urbworld Corportation Gel5 0.7mm black gel pen
\n・AHE-0005M4-PNJ - 80 page formatted notebook 
\n・AHE-0005M4-UM - This manual
\n
\n・If any of the supplied materials are broken, thrown away, missing, or otherwise have to be replaced, they can be ordered from our site under the product codes above.
\n
\nThis is generally best done with a partner, but can also be done with anyone you want.
\nThis is a prolonged experiment. Any portable electronics involved (such as camera) should be plugged in.
"
,,40)
}
PRINTFORMW Double checking that you have everything you need, you flip again
{
CALL PRINT_LETTER(
@"--- BEFORE USE ---
\n1. Insert the TransFlash storage card into the camera.
\n - The included card is good for up to 2 weeks of photos.
\n - When the TF card is full, the recording will stop and the camera will beep to indicate it needs a TF card with free space
\n - Alternative cards, up to 2TB as per TFEP (Extended Play) specifications are supported.
\n2. Screw the camera mount into the camera's tripod screw.  
\n3. Plug the included charger into an outlet and plug the USB-C end into the camera's USB-C port.
"
,,40)
}
PRINTFORML You open the memory card and open its small case, taking the TF card out.
PRINTFORML You grab the camera's power adapter, plug it into one of the outlets, and insert the end on the camera's USB port.
PRINTFORML After plugging the camera into the wall, you grab the small tripod and screw it into the bottom of the camera.
PRINTFORMW You press the power button and the camera lights up to life.
PRINTL
SETCOLOR C_GREEN
PRINTFORML 「                          」
PRINTFORML 「                          」
PRINTFORML 「          ACTMIX          」
PRINTFORML 「          by EFun         」
PRINTFORML 「        ACM-6310M2        」
PRINTFORML 「                          」
PRINTFORMW 「                          」
RESETCOLOR
PRINTFORML After a few seconds, the screen switches to a viewfinder.
PRINTFORML 「1080p 20K            PHOTO」
PRINTFORML 「                          」
PRINTFORML 「             -            」
PRINTFORML 「           -----          」
PRINTFORML 「             -            」
PRINTFORML 「F 2                       」
PRINTFORMW 「ISO 300          BAT 100\%+」
PRINTFORML There's several modes the camera can be at, including 「Photo」,「Video」,「Panaramic」, and the aformentioned「Timelapse」mode.
PRINTFORML You set the camera's mode to Timelapse.
PRINTFORML 「1080p 2WK     TIMELAPSE 1M」
PRINTFORML 「                          」
PRINTFORML 「             -            」
PRINTFORML 「           -----          」
PRINTFORML 「             -            」
PRINTFORML 「F 2                       」
PRINTFORMW 「ISO 300          BAT 100\%+」
PRINTL
PRINTFORMW You turn the page again
{
CALL PRINT_LETTER(
@"--- HOW TO RUN AN EXPERIMENT ---
\n1. Turn on the camera and set it to 「Timelapse」 mode.
\n2. Mount the camera to your desired position.
\n3. Place fresh meat into the jars. For the most comprehensive data possible the meat should be of different types (cow, pig, duck, fish).
\n4. Seal the jars and click on the camera's shutter. The camera will take a picture every one minute when it's recording.
\n5. It is best to check the jars at least once per day, but if you forgot, you can always look at the picture log.
\n6. Log the state of the meat using the notebook.
\nWhen the experiment is done, you can either offload the pictures to a FREAX (or derivative) PC or delete them.
\n
\n --- CLEANUP AND REUSE INSTRUCTIONS ---
\n・After the food rots and decays, dispose of the food outside in a garbage bin or incinerator.
\n・Wash jars throughly after use and dry outside in ventilated area. They will smell.
\n・Wash hands with soap and water.
"
,,40)
}
PRINTFORMW You set the glass jars slightly apart and place the camera.
;extended storage glass HOME-ESG-440AM8
ELSE
;else, checking the jars already
PRINTFORML You open the journal again and note the state of the meat.
ENDIF
DRAWLINE
YJ16_LineCount = LINECOUNT
DO
CLEARLINE LINECOUNT-YJ16_LineCount
FOR LOCAL, 0, 3
	PRINTFORM [{LOCAL}] Jar {LOCAL+1}: 
	IF YJ16_Item:LOCAL > -1
		PRINTFORM %ITEMNAME_TR(YJ16_Item:LOCAL)%
		IF YJ16_SeePart < YSSP16_MEAT_STATE(LOCAL)
			SETCOLOR C_YELLOW
			PRINTS "  New status!"
			RESETCOLOR
		ENDIF
		PRINTL
		PRINT 	
		SELECTCASE YSSP16_MEAT_STATE(LOCAL)
		CASE 0
		PRINTFORML The meat is fresh as it can be.
		CASE 1
		PRINTFORML The meat looks fine
		CASE 2
		PRINTFORML A faint dark layer of oxidization is present on the meat.
		CASE 3
		PRINTFORML The meat looks discolored.
		CASE 4
		PRINTFORML A slight green mold is now present on the meat.
		CASE 5
		PRINTFORML Significant amounts of green mold have taken over the meat.
		CASE 6
		PRINTFORML The meat is basically black with a bit of green.
		CASE 7
		PRINTFORML The meat has disintegrated into dust.
		ENDSELECT
	ELSE
		PRINTFORML Empty
	ENDIF
NEXT
DRAWLINE
PRINTFORML [882] - Throw away fully decayed
PRINTFORML [884] - Review Footage
PRINTFORML [999] - Exit
INPUT
YJ16_Input = RESULT
SELECTCASE YJ16_Input
CASE 0 TO 2
	IF YJ16_Item:YJ16_Input != -1
		IF YSSP16_MEAT_STATE() >= 7
			PRINTFORML You review the footage, note the changes and throw the disintegrated meat away
		    CALL YoujutsuLearningProgress(ARG,16,YSSP16_GET_XP(YJ16_Input))
			YJ16_Item:YJ16_Input = -1
			YJ16_Age:YJ16_Input = 0
			YJ16_SeePart:YJ16_Input = 0
			WAIT
		ELSE
			PRINTFORML Do you want to trash this meat?
			PRINTFORML Your footage will be reviewed before the meat is thrown away
		ENDIF
	ELSE
		PRINTFORML Select a meat to add.
		PRINTL
		FOR LOCAL,0,VARSIZE("ITEM")
			IF !YSSP16_IS_MEAT(LOCAL)
				CONTINUE
			ENDIF
			PRINTFORML [{LOCAL,4}] %ITEMNAME_TR(LOCAL)% ({ITEM:LOCAL}x)
		NEXT
		PRINTL
		PRINTFORML [-1] Cancel
		INPUT
		YJ16_Input:1 = RESULT
		IF YJ16_Input:1 == -1
			CONTINUE
		ELSEIF !YSSP16_IS_MEAT(YJ16_Input:1) 
			REUSELASTLINE Invalid input
			RESTART
		ENDIF
		PRINTFORML You add some %ITEMNAME_TR(YJ16_Input:1)% to the jar.
		CALL LOST_ITEM(ITEMNAME:(YJ16_Input:1), 1, 2)
		YJ16_Item:YJ16_Input = YJ16_Input:1
		YJ16_Age:YJ16_Input = TIME:1
		YJ16_SeePart:YJ16_Input = 0
	ENDIF
CASE 882
	LOCAL:1 = 0
	LOCAL:2 = 0
	FOR LOCAL,0,3
		IF YSSP16_MEAT_STATE(LOCAL) >= 7
			LOCAL:1 = 1
			LOCAL:2 += YSSP16_GET_XP(LOCAL)
			YJ16_Item:YJ16_Input = -1
			YJ16_Age:YJ16_Input = 0
			YJ16_SeePart:YJ16_Input = 0
		ELSE
			CONTINUE
		ENDIF
	NEXT
	IF LOCAL:1
		PRINTFORML You review the footage, note the changes and throw the disintegrated meat away
		CALL YoujutsuLearningProgress(ARG,16,LOCAL:2)
		WAIT
	ELSE
		PRINTFORMW No meat to throw away yet.
	ENDIF
CASE 884
	LOCAL:1 = 0
	LOCAL:2 = 0
	FOR LOCAL,0,3
		IF YJ16_Item:LOCAL != -1
			LOCAL:1 = 1
			LOCAL:2 += YSSP16_GET_XP(LOCAL)
			YJ16_SeePart:LOCAL = YSSP16_MEAT_STATE(LOCAL)
		ELSE
			CONTINUE
		ENDIF
	NEXT
	IF LOCAL:1 && LOCAL:2
		PRINTFORML You review the footage and find some new discoveries
		CALL YoujutsuLearningProgress(ARG,16,LOCAL:2)
		WAIT
	ELSEIF LOCAL:1
		PRINTFORMW You review the footage and but find nothing new
	ENDIF
CASE 999
RETURN
ENDSELECT
LOOP 1
;Jar 1: Empty
;Jar 2: Cow Meat
;	- The meat looks fine
;Jar 3: Human Meat
;	- The meat looks fine

@YSSP16_MEAT_STATE(ARG)
#FUNCTION
SIF !(YJ16_Age:ARG)
	RETURNF -1
SELECTCASE TIME_PROGRESS(YJ16_Age:ARG)
CASE IS < 90
;fresh
;0 to 90 minutes
RETURNF 0
CASE IS < 600
;fine
;90 minutes to 10 hours
RETURNF 1
CASE IS < 1440
;oxidized
;10 hours to 1 day
RETURNF 2
CASE IS < 2880
;discolored
;1 day to 2 days
RETURNF 3
CASE IS < 4320
;slightly moldy
;2 days to 3 days
RETURNF 4
CASE IS < 8640
;rotten
;3 days to 6 days
RETURNF 5
CASE IS < 11520
;decaying
;6 days to 8 days
RETURNF 6
CASEELSE
;disintegrated
;8 days+
RETURNF 7
ENDSELECT

@YSSP16_IS_MEAT(ARG)
#FUNCTION
RETURNF (INRANGE(ARG,1220,1230) || INRANGE(ARG,701,708)) && STRLENS(ITEMNAME_TR(ARG))

@YSSP16_GET_XP(ARG)
#FUNCTION
#DIM CONST POINTS = 20,45,90,150,200,350,500,1000
#DIM DYNAMIC PointToGet
#DIM DYNAMIC PL_LOOP
FOR PL_LOOP, YJ16_SeePart:ARG, YSSP16_MEAT_STATE(ARG)+1
	IF YJ16_SeePart:ARG < PL_LOOP
		PointToGet += POINTS:PL_LOOP
	ENDIF
NEXT
SELECTCASE YJ16_Item:ARG
CASE 701
	;pheasant
	TIMES PointToGet, 0.5
CASE 702
	;red meat
	TIMES PointToGet, 0.7
CASE 703
	;chicken meat
	TIMES PointToGet, 0.4
CASE 705
	;unknown meat
	TIMES PointToGet, 1.0
CASE 706
	;frog
	TIMES PointToGet, 0.75
CASE 707
	;fish
	TIMES PointToGet, 0.6
CASE 708
	;finest fish
	TIMES PointToGet, 1.2
CASE 1220
	;human
	TIMES PointToGet, 1.0
CASE 1221
	;youkai
	TIMES PointToGet, 1.1
CASE 1222
	;hermet
	TIMES PointToGet, 1.3
CASE 1223
	;divine spirit
	;tskumogami
	TIMES PointToGet, 1.5
CASE 1224
	;phantom
	TIMES PointToGet, 1.25
CASE 1225
	;fairy
	TIMES PointToGet, 0.7
CASE 1226
	;tskumogami
	TIMES PointToGet, 1.4
CASE 1227
	;oni
	TIMES PointToGet, 1.1
CASE 1228
	;hourai
	TIMES PointToGet, 2.0
CASE 1229
	;celestial
	TIMES PointToGet, 1.6
CASE 1230
	;tengu
	TIMES PointToGet, 1.15
CASEELSE
	;1.0x
ENDSELECT
RETURNF PointToGet

